{# =====================================================
   PLATFORM PILLARS — Website V2
   Structural home is the OLD homepage's "AI infrastructure, built to
   scale." pillar section — reskinned with glass-effect cards instead
   of the retired solid-blue/`sky` treatment (MASTER_DESIGN_SPEC.md
   §93/§114 retires that accent). Copy is reworked (not reused
   verbatim) to carry the Kore.ai 3-tier concept (Pre-built →
   Accelerators → Tailored/Platform), matching the new industry-first
   positioning in CONTENT_SUMMARY.md §1 rather than the old
   service-first "custom AI systems wired into your stack" framing
   the original cards used:
     1. Pre-built  (Kore's "Pre-built Applications")
     2. Accelerators + deploy discipline (Kore's "Application Accelerators")
     3. Scale to any use case (Kore's "Tailored Applications")

   3 cards only, by design — no "Own it completely" / infrastructure-
   ownership card. That claim belonged to the old service-first model
   (client owns the infra we build for them) and doesn't fit the
   current multi-tenant shared-platform model (CONTENT_SUMMARY.md §4/
   company-industry-context.md §4), so it was dropped rather than
   carried forward or replaced.

   Card 1's copy says "proven in production," not "already running in
   production" — deliberately avoids reading as a blanket live-status
   claim across all four verticals; only Education (Admizz) and
   Agencies (self-run + Mobilise) are confirmed live today, Healthcare
   is capability-led and Real Estate has no client yet
   (company-industry-context.md §3). Mirrors the same live-vs-
   capability distinction the Industry Showcase section above already
   makes explicit.
   ===================================================== #}
